<article class="env-lemma" id="04QU">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04QU">Lemma <span data-tag="04QU">35.22.2</span>.</a> Let $\tau \in \{ fpqc, fppf, syntomic, smooth, {\acute{e}tale}, Zariski\} $. Let $\mathcal{P}$ be a property of morphisms which is $\tau $ local on the target. Let $f : X \to Y$ have property $\mathcal{P}$. For any morphism $Y' \to Y$ which is flat, resp. flat and locally of finite presentation, resp. syntomic, resp. étale, resp. an open immersion, the base change $f' : Y' \times _ Y X \to Y'$ of $f$ has property $\mathcal{P}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is true because we can fit $Y' \to Y$ into a family of morphisms which forms a $\tau $-covering. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>